  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Connecticut received $16B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $15.7B of that total. Award activity included 22,633 contracts with an average award size of $708K, and obligations were down 54.4% year over year. Past fiscal-year totals show variability: FY21 was $18.4B, FY22 was $22.3B, FY23 was $26B, FY24 was $20B, and FY25 was $35.1B. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $6.9B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the second largest industry at $3.2B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $1.7B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the top vendor at $8.6B, followed by RTX CORPORATION at $3.7B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $2.8B. Other notable vendors include HAMILTON SUNDSTRAND CORPORATION at $99.5M and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $61.6M. The top ten buying agencies list includes the Department of Veterans Affairs at $109M and the Department of Homeland Security at $106M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Connecticut?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $15.7B. Engineering Services is the largest industry, receiving $6.9B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is the largest vendor, with $8.6B in obligations. Overall obligations for FY2026 to date are $16B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 54.4% year over year. Total obligations for FY2026 to date are $16B compared with prior fiscal-year totals such as $35.1B in FY25 and $20B in FY24. The number of awards for FY2026 to date is 22,633 with an average award size of $708K."
      }
    ]
